---

SOX Protocol is a runtime-agnostic peer messaging protocol for LLM agents,
providing channel primitives (pub/sub, direct messages, groups, threads,
presence, ACK/NACK) and a speculative-execute-while-awaiting-clarification
discipline for multi-agent systems.

